1. End-to-end headless test system for dev confidence
    [ ] 'content/ports_adapters/adapters.py': Implement 'ScriptedIOBridge'
        - Feeds pre-recorded key sequences, ending with a graceful exit action
        - Captures screen frames and clipboard outputs into a test report file
    [ ] 'content/clanker.py': Support test mode flag
        - Check CLI arguments (`--test`) to select `ScriptedIOBridge` over standard `IOBridge`
        - Run rest of application setup and execution pipeline unchanged
    [ ] 'tests/e2e_harness.py': Create E2E test harness
        - Run app in test mode across clankerized and un-clankerized scenarios
        - Parse report file, verify UI states and prompt compilations
        - Prompt dev with interactive summary and pass/fail verdict
    [ ] 'ship.sh': Add optional quality gate integration
        - Execute test harness as the first ship gate, blocking commit/push on exit code 1
    - Finally P/A architecture becomes useful


2. clankerization of a project can represent the much talked about repo contract by the content it creates
    - it should check 'does any of the content exist'?
        - if so dont do anything, complain to user
    - only if coast clear should it create the stuff in repo root
        - '.clanker' dir and its internal stuff
        - 'README.md' -> #empty
        - 'content' -> no members

3. i should be able to add more than just filesets as named bottom level sets.
    - we have 3 resolvers that deal with files
        - md resolver has fallback to shared logic, uses Filelist which contain File 
            - this should become a bottom level thing
        - repo and manifest resolvers both use Filesets
            - this is already a bottom level thing. do Fileset class need an attr to say source? 
                - It can default to pud
                - and optionally by some flag var work off of shared instead
            - then improves semantics of yaml?

4. Validation / complaints
    - manifest resolver must check if fileset is declared in pud_cfg with fallback to shared_cfg
        - so shared_cfg can declare defaults for it, which the pud_cfg can override
        - if not present, then complain

5. Make use of latest architectural work in ingestion module
    - simplify EC and 'Report' for now, lets just have str msgs for ez

