    - turns into a pipeline refactor. oh well
    - we have the righthand side of the screen to put info on. will be baller, only green (black) grass

7. Non IDE / linter import strats: BUFF importance of this, as LLMs typically run lower than 3.14 version of python, and cannot compensate.
    - goals:
        - We dont have huge import blocks in all the numerous files, eating up precious llm context
        - all types used in a file are always imported (explicitly or via kleene)
            - this goes for typehints too
        - the inverse. no dangling imports allowed
            - but what abt * imports?
    - something about python v 3.14 vs older versions - a clue!
    - i added instruction to prune in the do-mode.md file, so it gets done bit by bit at least

8. Mull 'ExceptionPolicy'
    - its purpose is essentially to classify ex that core does not deal with
    - and to format the msgs that get printed in main

9. Follow up prompts
    - to pass the next step of workflow
        - plan into do into backlog management
    - reduce token waste
